  "source": "Unverified seed (S10, 19 Oct 2026): from docs/RULES.md draft v0.2, ledger decisions D25, D28, D29, D30 and S34, and the owner's board images of 18 and 19 Oct 2026.",
  "notes": "Game state, not piece data (S17, src/game/game.ts): its first move is a5 to e5, which opens the Coast (coast.2p.initiation); the repeat limit (tail.repeatLimit); either player may move it in 2-player games, and it never captures a piece of the player moving it. In 3-player games it is the Dragon's King while it is active, and turns to stone when checkmated: game state (S56, src/game/three.ts, decision 0016). In 3-player games all other Coast pieces are the Dragon's own, so non-coast-pieces captures any enemy piece. Its way off the Coast in 3-player games (coast.3p.exit) is a square rule, as for the other Coast pieces (S68); with tail.3p.movement = two-player-path it only stands on A5, E5 and I5, so the rule never stops it. Its 3-player slide (tail.3p.movement = like-dragon-head) has one move per tail.3p.range option (S84, decision 0023): same-as-heads reads dragonHead.range, 1 to 8 are its own."
}
